sqlparse-rust incorporates no upstream source code: it is an independent
Rust implementation of the SQL lexing / statement-splitting / grouping /
formatting behavior described by the upstream project below. The
pure-Python fallback (`sqlparse/_pure.py`) is a byte-identical copy of the
upstream 0.6.0 `sqlparse` package, used when the Rust extension is
unavailable or the input is outside the kernel's exact domain (and as the
correctness oracle for the equivalence suite):

